= Safety factor — Simple =

A '''safety factor''' is an engineering margin used when designing and checking a structure or other device.

Engineers may design something to resist more than the greatest load they expect it to see during use. The extra margin helps account for uncertainties.

Different standards use different definitions and numbers. A factor by itself does not prove a structure is safe: designers also need to check different ways it could fail, materials, testing and the conditions of use.

